SWEET AMP DSP (patch 0169, plan A9e), boot-arg sweetaoc=6 + sweetamp=1: sweetaoc=5 plus the CS35L41 HALO DSP firmware load of both amps.
New bsd/dev/sweet_amp_dsp.h (sequence + cites in its header); sweet_amp.h: DSP allowlist, CS-held bursts, A9 hook; sweet_amp.c:
sweet_amp_dsp_arm (/chosen/memory-map AMPFW, tools/pack_ampfw.py, lengths + sha256 pinned); sweet_aoc.c / sweet_aoc_start.c: mode 6.
Per amp (L, then R): pre-check, cs35l41_dsp_init writes (RX/TX RATE := 1, RX5..8 SRC), the 6 wmfw regions, the HALO id header +
algorithm list, the .bin blocks (L / R- file), every byte read back; 0166 TDM config; MPU config, CCM_CORE_CTRL start (0x201); heartbeat
window 1, 0167 stream + PLL poll, window 2; WDT off, CCM EN off (read back); AOC close; 0158 restore. PWR_CTRL1 never written; no
SOFT_RESET, no mailbox write, no amp enable. Pass "SWEET AMP DSP: fw loaded l,r (id 400a4 rev 1d00), halo running l,r", else
"SWEET AMP DSP: stopped l=<stage> r=<stage> ...". No Linux code or table copied. Host test shim/amp_xnu_host_test.c. BUILT, UNRUN.

