+ * amps, start of the core, a bounded check that it runs, then stop. Included by sweet_amp.h (after the SPI layer, before the A9 run); pure logic,
+ * also compiled by shim/amp_xnu_host_test.c against a fake amp with DSP memory. No Linux code or table is copied: register addresses, values and
+ * file-format constants only (as sweet_cs_dsp.h of patch 0166, which parses the files here).
+ *
+ * Files (vendor.img /vendor/firmware, docs/research/46 (a) 8; names: AMP wm_adsp.c:1848-1849 "%s-%s-%s.wmfw" = cs35l41-dsp1-spk-prot.wmfw for
+ * both amps; :2596-2602 "%s-%s-%s.bin", with the DT cirrus,tuning-has-prefix and sound-name-prefix "R" on cs35l41@1 only -> L cs35l41-dsp1-spk-prot.bin,
+ * R R-cs35l41-dsp1-spk-prot.bin), pinned by length + sha256 below and in tools/pack_ampfw.py; delivered as /chosen/memory-map AMPFW (container
+ * AMPFWV01 of tools/pack_ampfw.py, the pack_wlanfw layout). The blobs never go in git.
+ *
+ * Sequence, stock = Google amplifiers 33976d7 (AMP) cs35l41.c + snd_soc_wm_adsp/wm_adsp.c, Linux v6.18 where it differs:
+ *  probe   cs35l41_dsp_init (AMP cs35l41.c:3707-3766, after the CCM := 0 of :4401 that patch 0158 already writes): cs35l41_fs_errata_patch
+ *          DSP1_RX1..8_RATE / TX1..8_RATE := 1 (:3688-3705, :3730-3732; v6.18 cs35l41-lib.c:680-697, :1497-1508), DSP1_RX5..8_SRC := VPMON, CLASSH,
+ *          TEMPMON, RSVD (:3743-3766). Each written word is read back here.
+ *  load    DSP1 Preloader PRE_PMU -> wm_adsp_boot_work (wm_adsp.c:3041-3096; HALO has no enable_memory / enable_core, ops :4620-4634):
+ *          wm_adsp_load (:1826-2010): every memory region of the wmfw as one raw write to region_to_reg (:867-883); wm_halo_setup_algs
+ *          (:2517-2576): the id header (wmfw_halo_id_hdr, v6.18 wmfw.h:76-106) and the algorithm list (wmfw_halo_alg_hdr :126-132) read from XM
